chapter.v:
	“And inasmuch 

	 as the king saw a watcher, a holy one, coming down from heaven and saying, ‘Chop down the tree and destroy it, but leave its stump and roots in the earth, bound with a band of iron and bronze in the tender grass of the field; let it be wet with the dew of heaven, and let him graze with the beasts of the field, till seven times pass over him’;
 [2 Cor. 6:16; Eph. 3:17; [1 John 2:24]; Rev. 3:20;]
